Now the RatingService: processes all unrated events.

```
final class RatingService {
  __construct(em, BillingCalculator $calc, PriceRepository, ProviderRepository)

  public function rateAll(): array {
    $unrated = $this->events->findUnrated();
    $rated = 0; $unratedLeft = 0;
    $stderr = [];
    foreach ($unrated as $e) {
      $price = findApplicable(provider, model, ts)
      if ($price === null) { $unratedLeft++; $stderr[] = "UNRATED {$e->getProvider()}/{$e->getProviderRequestId()} {$e->getTs()->format('c')} no_price"; continue; }
      $provider = $price->getProvider();
      $off = $provider->offPeak();
      $cost = $calc->calculate(...tokens..., $price->getUnit(), $price->getRates(), $off, $e->getTs());
      $e->markRated($cost, $price->getCurrency(), $price->getValidFrom());
      $rated++;
    }
    $em->flush();
    return ['rated'=>$rated,'unrated'=>$unratedLeft,'stderr'=> $stderr];
  }
}
```

The ts format in stderr should match ts format. Task example: `UNRATED <provider>/<provider_request_id> <ts> no_price`. ts is presumably the event's ts in ISO. I'll output the event's ts as ISO8601 Z. Let me use format 'Y-m-d\TH:i:s\Z'. Good.

